---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/react`;

const neutralHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="banner"
  data-tone="neutral"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <p class="sk-alert__title">Mantenimiento programado</p>
    <div class="sk-alert__description">
      On Sunday from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC the panel will be read-only.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sk-alert__actions">
    <button
      class="sk-alert__dismiss"
      type="button"
      aria-label="Cerrar alerta"
    >
      <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>`;

const bannerHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="banner"
  data-tone="info"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <span class="sk-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-sk-icon="info"></span>
  </span>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <p class="sk-alert__title">New version</p>
    <div class="sk-alert__description">
      An update is available.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>`;

const accentHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="accent"
  data-tone="warning"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <span class="sk-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-sk-icon="warning"></span>
  </span>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <p class="sk-alert__title">Your plan expires in 3 days</p>
    <div class="sk-alert__description">
      Choose a plan so as not to interrupt your deployments.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sk-alert__actions">
    <a class="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/billing">Ver planes</a>
    <button
      class="sk-alert__dismiss"
      type="button"
      aria-label="Cerrar alerta"
    >
      <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>`;

const inlineHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="inline"
  data-tone="success"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <span class="sk-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-sk-icon="success"></span>
  </span>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <div class="sk-alert__description">Your changes have been saved.</div>
  </div>
</div>`;

const neutralReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

<Alert
  tone="neutral"
  title="Mantenimiento programado"
  onDismiss={() => hide()}
>
  On Sunday from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC the panel will be read-only.
</Alert>;`;

const bannerReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

<Alert tone="info" title="New version">
  An update is available.
</Alert>;`;

const accentReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

<Alert
  onDismiss={() => hide()}
  actions={
    <a className="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/billing">
      Ver planes
    </a>
  }
  presentation="accent"
  title="Your plan expires in 3 days"
  tone="warning"
>
  Choose a plan so as not to interrupt your deployments.
</Alert>;`;

const inlineReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

<Alert presentation="inline" tone="success">
  Your changes have been saved.
</Alert>;`;
---

<Base title="Alert" description="Alert: Persistent inline message with tone (including neutral), accessible announcement and React component.">
  <h1>Alert</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Alert is an inline message that remains in the layout for the duration of its condition. Unlike
    Toast, transient, and mounted in a floating region, Alert lives in the flow of content.
  </p>

  <h2>Tonos</h2>
  <p>
    The tone decides whether the panel is painted with semantic color.
    <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code> and <code>danger</code> color the
    message. Only <code>danger</code> is advertised as <code>role="alert"</code> (assertive); the rest
    use <code>role="status"</code> (polite).
  </p>
  <p>
    The four read a <strong>feedback role</strong>, never the accent: the tone says what happened, like this
    which cannot change when the brand changes. <code>info</code> had its own ramp just in the
    decision 26 (<code>docs/decisiones/0026-info-es-un-rol-de-feedback-no-el-acento.md</code>); before
    It read <code>accent</code>, and a magenta mark painted each information notice magenta.
  </p>

  <h3>Neutral</h3>
  <p>
    The default: surface and edge, without semantic painting. It exists for when the color should not be
    the prominent sign, the text (and, in a
    <a href="/en/components/toast">Toast</a>, the fact of floating and disappearing) already load the message.
    Use it in ordinary notices, short confirmations or any case where you paint the dashboard
    “success” or “info” would add urgency that the content does not have.
  </p>
  <Showcase html={neutralHtml} react={neutralReact} label="Alert neutral" />

  <h2>Presentaciones</h2>
  <p>The presentation decides the visual weight, not the urgency.</p>

  <h3>Banner</h3>
  <p>The full panel is for a condition that needs a title and explanation along with the affected content.</p>
  <Showcase html={bannerHtml} react={bannerReact} label="Alert banner" />

  <h3>Acento</h3>
  <p>The sidebar preserves the tone signal and lets a recovery action take center stage.</p>
  <Showcase html={accentHtml} react={accentReact} label="Alert acento" />

  <h3>Inline</h3>
  <p>Without a panel or border, a short confirmation accompanies a block that already has its own structure.</p>
  <Showcase html={inlineHtml} react={inlineReact} label="Alert inline" />

  <h2>Anatomy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>sk-alert__icon</code> is decorative and only appears when it provides a visual signal.</li>
    <li><code>sk-alert__content</code> groups optional title and description.</li>
    <li><code>sk-alert__actions</code> hosts actions that belong to the consumer; the optional closure lives there.</li>
    <li><code>data-tone</code> acepta <code>neutral</code> (default), <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code> o <code>danger</code>.</li>
    <li><code>data-presentation</code> acepta <code>banner</code> (default), <code>accent</code> o <code>inline</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of each example. <code>onDismiss</code> is optional: without it, the close button is not drawn.</p>
</Base>
